// expect-error: L0102
// A character that starts no token is a token of its own, and the lexer goes on after it.
// Two of them side by side are two tokens, and a letter outside ASCII is one whole character.
// The longest punctuation wins, so `===` is `==` then `=`, and `- >` is two tokens.
fn f() {
    x := 1 @@ 2 # 3
    café := $ ~ ^ ` \ ; &
    y := a === b - > c)(
}
